{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}

O [G]come, all ye [D]faithful, [G]joyful and tri[D]umphant,
O [Em]come ye, O [D]come ye to [A]Bethle[D]hem;
[G]Come and be[C]hold [G]Him, [Em]born the [C]King of [D]angels;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [G]come, let us [Em]adore [D]Him,
O [C]come, let [Am]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.

Sing, [G]choirs of an[D]gels, [G]sing in exul[D]tation,
[Em]Sing, all ye [D]citizens of [A]heav'n a[D]bove;
[G]Glory to [C]God, [G]  [Em]glory [C]in the [D]highest;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [G]come, let us [Em]adore [D]Him,
O [C]come, let [Am]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.

Yea, [G]Lord, we greet [D]Thee, [G]born this happy [D]morning,
[Em]Jesus, to [D]Thee be [A]glory [D]giv'n;
[G]Word of the [C]Fa[G]ther, [Em]now in [C]flesh ap[D]pearing;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [G]come, let us [Em]adore [D]Him,
O [C]come, let [Am]us a[D]dore [C]Him,
[G]Christ [D]the [G]Lord.
